    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "Amidst the documented month-over-month data increase, experts note a quantitative shift in enforcement metrics along the U.S. border. The border enforcement agency apprehended over 8,200 individuals in March, a rise from the prior month's 6,598, a trend observers of quantitative patterns attribute to a seasonal climatic variable. However, corroborated long-term statistical context shows year-to-date figures remain near multi-decade lows, an enforcement policy outcome of ongoing asylum and deportation measures.",
      "source": {
