    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "The legislative impasse on funding allocation persists, even as data interpreters analyze the recent spike in apprehensions. While the stated environmental factor of milder spring weather correlates with the increase, the core issue is a decisional paralysis preventing policy clarity among government officials. This stalemate obscures the factual analysis needed to contextualize the border security effect, leaving the immigration statistics in a state of political limbo.",
