    {
      "id": "p3",
      "text": "Policy decision-makers remain deadlocked over funding for a federal law enforcement agency, even as security analysts present a verified statistical observation of rising apprehensions. This political deadlock overshadows the crucial context: overall policy outcome maintaining historical baseline numbers, despite a recent numerical change. The focus on a political stalemate obscuring factual analysis risks ignoring the larger corroborated long-term statistical context of border security.",
